      "baseRefOid": "cced011659d48877b8b73b8a85796815234cf741",
      "body": "The public engine returned the setting polar intersection for some charts while the site repaired it locally. This candidate moves the validated correction before house assembly and adds Cartesian geometry and public-entrypoint regressions. It also rejects unconverged Placidus cusps, invalid or ambiguous resolved dates, missing timezone inputs, historical year coercion, unbounded return scans, and duplicate exact sample-boundary crossings.\n\nCandidate: `@zodiacs/engine@0.1.1-rc.1`, source `03bf77990f3014b9125eed4976d7a41200aac80d`. Packed SHA-256: `f95c887deedb55f64b185ed4dd406b580b6d3287656ab5ec0557215fc02e5d17`. Public npm engine/widgets lookups returned 404 on 2026-09-07; no publication performed. The optional read-only ownership SDK is unchanged.\n\nValidation: 295 tests across 26 files passed on Node 20.20.2 and 22.23.2; workspace lint/typecheck/build, format, checksum, neutrality, export smoke, pack dry run and package contents passed. The exact tarball installed in a clean directory: public ESM examples, declarations, invalid inputs, notices and absence of React/ownership SDK passed under Node 22.23.2 / TypeScript 5.9.3. The clean consumer audit reports zero vulnerabilities. Existing independent site fixture policies are preserved, and public-package node/polar comparisons pass on Node 22 and 24. TypeDoc regenerated from source.\n\nInitial package commands hit a sandbox cache permission error; a separate writable cache resolved it. The whole-workspace production audit reports 59 advisories (21 high) in the existing app/example tree. This PR does not upgrade that unrelated tree or claim those applications are release-ready.\n\nAcceptance: A02/A03 and bounded A04 work. This draft is stacked on PR #5 to keep the correction reviewable. PR #5's explicit do-not-merge/do-not-publish hold remains. Required review, publication authority, comprehensive numerical scope and later hosted/privacy gates are not satisfied by this PR. No human practitioner or legal signoff is claimed.\n\nThe companion site draft PR [#415](https://github.com/ZodiacsOfficial/site/pull/415) (`codex/platform-stage-a`) pins the immutable candidate and removes its repair, retaining the 0.1.0 archive and legacy saved-chart migration. Site verification passed: 4,431 tests / 404 files, check/build/schema/bundle gates, independent references, 18 mobile/desktop captures and chart-sharing/developer-browser flows. Durable platform records are in the companion change. Rollback: revert the candidate pin/adapter change in the site; do not overwrite a packed or published artifact.\n\nRemote checks on this stacked PR: primary SDK Vercel preview passed; auxiliary sdk-zodia-launch failed with the existing missing-public-output configuration. GitHub SDK/App workflows only target PRs into main, so they did not run on this expansion-based PR. Required commands were run locally; this is not a claim of new remote CI success.\n",
