    {
      "baseRefName": "codex/platform-stage-a",
      "baseRefOid": "03bf77990f3014b9125eed4976d7a41200aac80d",
      "body": "A rejected GeoNames index or shard request stayed cached for the lifetime of a client, so a later explicit preload/search could not recover after the transport recovered. This change evicts only the matching failed promise and preserves its original rejection reason. Current callers still share one request, successful/unrelated cache entries remain, and a later explicit call can retry. There is no automatic retry loop, backoff or new cancellation API.\n\nThis is a separate `@zodiacs/engine@0.1.1-rc.2` candidate. Source `0da0941e23035df3be95e5aa40f4f270222b57dd`; frozen artifact/evidence commit `abefc7c347ed22708a6743713d58c843d7166d8e`. Archive `artifacts/zodiacs-engine-0.1.1-rc.2.tgz`, SHA-256 `b5c0c63bddc8c1ccfc717551bdd57b1bfe7c439568851780575c8586456e0826`, 18 files / 21,946 packed bytes. The site's rc.1 and public starter rc.2 remain unchanged; this PR does not upgrade them or replace any existing artifact. README, changelog, version and generated TypeDoc match this new candidate.\n\nValidation: eight new regression failures reproduced against baseline; all **305 workspace tests / 27 files** pass on Node 20 and 22. Required lint, typecheck, format, registry checksum, full build, export smoke, pack dry-run, package contents, neutrality and TypeDoc gates pass. Two actual clean consumers install the exact tarball without workspace links and compile public imports with TypeScript 5.9.3; public examples, optional-dependency isolation and packed geo retry behavior pass on Node 20/22. The isolated consumer audit reports zero advisories. A 96-case synthetic public-chart comparison with rc.1 has identical mathematical output after excluding engineVersion; this is version parity, not independent accuracy validation.\n\nA second real tool-backed reviewer passed 11 strict-unhandled-rejection probes, including immediate concurrent retry waves, synchronous transport throws, delayed JSON rejection, non-Error reasons and a reentrant transport demonstrating stale-eviction protection. This is model-assisted internal review, not human/external approval. Structurally invalid but parseable JSON remains a confirmed pre-existing limitation; this fix covers rejected transport, unsuccessful HTTP and JSON-parsing operations. Clearing healthy caches after arbitrary consumer errors would be a different policy.\n\nStacked on held draft #6 (`codex/platform-stage-a`). Existing SDK GitHub CI triggers only for PRs targeting main, so this stacked PR has local required-gate evidence rather than a claimed successful CI run. SDK #5 remains explicitly do-not-merge/do-not-publish. No npm publication, main merge, production deployment, account request, live GeoNames request, outreach, spending or external adoption. Optional read-only ownership SDK, root dependencies and lockfile are preserved. Exact commands, frozen package, logs, receipts and review limits are in `docs/platform/`. Acceptance: bounded A02/A03 reliability follow-up; complete portable receipts and broader release review remain open.\n",
