    {
      "baseRefName": "codex/platform-geonames-schema",
      "baseRefOid": "84897ffb6e044469875d381bdc0acbd39c995ffb",
      "body": "Correct typed `no-time` and `polar-fallback` birth inputs previously duplicated result flags and could not create a receipt. This candidate preserves the five-value public type, validates supplied assertions, and produces canonical flags once. It also captures validated public/civil settings before use, closing inconsistent `resolveBirth` validation and getter substitution paths.\n\nDraft stacked on #9. Engine **0.1.1-rc.5**, source **97f5e8d01828f4b85ffa845825dee9acff4695e4**. The 23-file immutable [review artifact](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ZodiacsOfficial/sdk/333369256af683c560603dd1e6411dd7a07adb1f/artifacts/zodiacs-engine-0.1.1-rc.5.tgz) was anonymously downloaded and matches SHA-256 `1809c1686843a6be148eb185535e32059a20c35896e29ccfc7583a6b2738da65` (36,065 bytes).\n\nKnown duplicate claims collapse up to a documented 64-entry raw limit. Malformed/private/contradictory flags reject with fixed errors. Supplied Charts receive flag/house metadata consistency checks and shallow normalization only; canonical identity and numerical arrays remain intact. Ordinary Saturn inputs add zero natal calculations; an explicit raw polar assertion adds one to verify actual fallback before scanning. Numerical formulas, receipt schema, internal computation, site/starter pins, ownership SDK and old archives are unchanged.\n\nValidation: 562 tests / 31 files on Node 20 and 22; all required workspace build/type/lint/format/checksum/neutrality/export/content/dry-pack and TypeDoc gates; two fresh packed consumers with public types and receipt/flags controls; 480 rc.4\u2192rc.5 chart parity cases plus 480 derived/duplicate echo controls; 14 independent adversarial controls. Isolated consumer audit: zero. Original 61-failure baseline, corrected test harness attempts and inherited npm-cache pack failure are retained. Stacked SDK CI does not run under the existing main-only workflow; no passing CI is claimed.\n\nActual Chrome 152 packed-browser acceptance passes 26/26 checks, including 14 runtime groups: all 23 installed members match, optional module graphs remain isolated, receipt/civil/flags/Saturn controls pass offline, observed fetch/storage and cookies are zero. The initial harness socket-length failure and exact final inputs/results/capture/trace are retained; owned resources are closed.\n\nTime flags remain caller claims. Precomputed numerical values are not authenticated; same-realm executable getters/proxies are not sandboxed. Finite parity is not independent astronomical accuracy. SDK #5's explicit **do not merge / do not publish** and required human/release review remain. This is a tested draft candidate, not npm publication, production deployment or external adoption. Rollback uses the prior immutable rc.4 artifact; never overwrite candidate bytes.\n\n[Source, before/after failures, commands, raw receipts and limits](https://github.com/ZodiacsOfficial/sdk/blob/785e3ea154c28e890ecc97ce2284ee3e9f48a4a7/docs/platform/EVIDENCE.md#public-flags-and-civil-settings-candidate).\n",
